position":"1788525385288130001-f03095d9-2f26-41fe-b327-a731c711bef1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3ddff1f24d923816e9b6203b10b99e73bfcc849969ddc64922ae739653dcb20b","event_uuid":"0b97133c-0d68-431d-a785-2b7a347ce8ce","position":{"commit_sha":"806897aea88b8eeb34b81a66ebbebb8c125b7f38","position":"1788525911131675001-0b97133c-0d68-431d-a785-2b7a347ce8ce"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d0cafeb34a85bcf4610f6a5e2690465f7e72710c6af9f0a6b6fccae8920d8fcc","event_uuid":"f09b9b1a-75c6-44d0-883c-5fc1d37d92fe","position":{"commit_sha":"a587ca7d9394bad098f72f0cb639c943c66c0ffe","position":"1788526230607632001-f09b9b1a-75c6-44d0-883c-5fc1d37d92fe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"45555f458d4edffb81a22866facd30aa33acb9496782133fe5a6f746b41cf085","event_uuid":"9bb57191-fb13-4f1a-b8c2-a0e84e9f03ff","position":{"commit_sha":"e2609604c4fa43855c32be214967c605d9ec4a37","position":"1788526242415899001-9bb57191-fb13-4f1a-b8c2-a0e84e9f03ff"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788318486025525038,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4c7b58ce-1776-427f-b6be-708552f53190","relation":"blocks","target_id":"a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87"},{"link_uuid":"806d2ab8-4323-430e-8138-e71dab083fe3","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6532-afd1-2beb-4f11"},{"link_uuid":"29f18fdb-f063-4d0e-9774-b1421a81886c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"be55-cb13-a241-4382"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`.github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml` runs its live tier on a weekly cron across every\ndataset-bearing spec, bounded only by `REBAR_EVAL_MAX_CASES: \"12\"` per spec, with no dollar\nceiling in that lane (its comment: \"Hard dollar caps live at the provider dashboard\").\n\nLetting the criteria covered by this epic join that sweep would multiply its per-run call\ncount several-fold every week, in perpetuity, and would grow again with each criterion\nadded later. The cron is also the wrong instrument for these fixtures: they exist to catch a\ncriterion-rubric regression, and a rubric regression arrives with a commit rather than with\nthe passage of time.\n\n## Approach\n\nExecute a criterion's fixtures when that criterion's rubric changes.\n\nThe selection is a rebar operation, not a CI feature: a shared engine function\n(`src/rebar/llm/evals/changed_criteria.py`) maps a changed-file set to the criterion ids\nwhose rubric files appear in it. It does NOT reimplement the criterion→rubric-path rule: it\nREUSES the prior-art primitive\n`rebar.llm.evals.fixture_selection.rubric_path(criterion_id, *, repo_root, gate_key='plan_review')`,\nwhich already resolves a logical id through `criterion_prompt_id` and `get_prompt`'s\noverride-wins ordering. For every id in `criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')`\nit resolves `rubric_path`, makes it repo-relative, and intersects that set with the changed\nfiles. This mirrors the code-review precedent `code_review.registry.glob_triggered_overlays` /\n`project_criterion_applies`, which likewise map a `changed_files` set to criterion ids.\n\n**Both rubric storage conventions are covered because `rubric_path` resolves both** — the\npackaged `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_<id>.md` and a `.rebar/prompts/plan-review-<id>.md`\nproject override (which wins). A changed path of rubric shape that maps to no effective\ncriterion's resolved rubric is UNMAPPED: named on stderr rather than skipped, selection still\nexits 0.\n\n**Range → changed files** reuses the existing `git diff --name-only <ref>..HEAD` plumbing\nshape already in the repo (`plan_review.drift_floor._drifted_paths`), not a second convention.\n\n**CLI surface and the argparse contract.** The existing `criteria eval` verb takes a REQUIRED\npositional `criterion_id` and returns exit 2 when it is empty/missing (`docs/exit-codes.md`).\nThis story makes the positional OPTIONAL and MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE with a new `--changed-since\n<ref>` flag: exactly one of {positional id, `--changed-since <ref>`} must be given. The bare\n`criteria eval` with NEITHER still returns 2, so the documented \"empty or missing id → 2\"\ncontract is preserved for that form. `docs/exit-codes.md` is updated in the same change to\ndocument the new mode: `criteria eval --changed-since <ref>` prints the selected criterion ids\n(sorted, one per line) and exits 0; an unmappable rubric-shaped path is named on stderr and\nstill exits 0.\n\n**Select-then-run.** The positional `criteria eval <id>` form is unchanged (always live). The\nnew `--changed-since` form prints the selection unconditionally, then runs each selected\ncriterion live ONLY when the `agents` extra + credentials are present; with no model configured\nit is selection-only and issues no model call (a non-rubric range exits 0 with no model call).\n\n**Portability.** The trigger is operation-linked: a developer (or a no-CI project) runs the\ncommand locally against any git range and gets the same selection; the workflow job is a thin\ncaller. The command shells out to nothing POSIX-specific and takes its repo root from the\nexisting resolution path.\n\n**CI trigger classification and ref derivation.** The new job is added to `prompt-eval.yml`.\nThe `pull_request` trigger is INCLUDED (a rubric edit arrives on a PR — the case this job\nexists for) passing `--changed-since ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}`; the `push`\ntrigger is INCLUDED for ordinary branches (passing `--changed-since ${{ github.event.before }}`)\nand EXCLUDED for `main`, `feature/**` and `tickets` via the existing `branches-ignore`; the\nweekly `schedule` trigger is EXCLUDED for the new job — the point of this child. No trigger is\nNO_FILTER. The job is non-blocking (`continue-on-error`) and same-repo-only.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe shared changed-rubric selection function (reusing `rubric_path`), its CLI flag with the\noptional/mutually-exclusive positional, the `docs/exit-codes.md` update, and the workflow job\nthat calls it. The existing weekly live sweep keeps its current spec set.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Changing the weekly cron's behavior for the specs it already covers.\n- Making the new job a required or blocking check; it stays non-blocking like the existing\n  live tier.\n- Any dollar-ceiling mechanism inside GitHub Actions.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nAdditive: one new engine function, one new CLI flag (the positional becomes optional but the\nexisting `criteria eval <id>` invocation is byte-compatible), one `docs/exit-codes.md` row\nupdate, one new workflow job. The offline tier (the only required check) and the weekly live\ntier are untouched. Back-out is deleting the job, the flag, and the doc row; no persisted\nstate, no format change.\n\n## Testing\n\nA real CLI subprocess against seeded temporary git repositories exercises the selection across\na rubric-touching range, a non-rubric range, and an unmappable rubric path (the subprocess tier\nis required for the argument parsing, git range resolution and exit codes). A unit test covers\nthe workflow's resolved spec list; the existing actionlint node covers workflow validity.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A range touching `plan_review_T8.md` and `plan_review_G6.md` selects exactly the\n      criterion ids `T8` and `G6`; verified by a `pytest` subprocess test asserting the\n      printed selection against a seeded temporary repository.\n- [x] A range touching no rubric file selects nothing, exits `0`, and issues no model call;\n      verified by the same subprocess test asserting an empty selection and `exit code` 0\n      with no model configured.\n- [x] A rubric path matching no registry criterion is named on stderr rather than skipped\n      silently, and selection still exits `0`; verified by `pytest` asserting the warning text\n      for a seeded `plan_review_bogus.md`.\n- [x] `criteria eval` with NEITHER a positional id NOR `--changed-since` still exits `2`,\n      preserving the documented contract; verified by `pytest` asserting exit code 2.\n- [x] Wiring the change-triggered live-eval path for this epic's criteria does NOT enroll\n      them into the weekly live sweep: after this change the weekly sweep's resolved spec\n      list still excludes the epic's prompt ids (they run on rubric change only, never on the\n      weekly cron), so the new path adds a trigger without widening the weekly sweep; verified\n      by `pytest` asserting the intersection of the epic's prompt ids and the weekly sweep's\n      resolved spec is empty.\n- [x] When the `--changed-since` ref range is uncomputable — a branch's first push, where\n      `github.event.before` is the all-zeros SHA — selection treats it as 'no prior ref',\n      selects nothing, exits `0`, and notes it on stderr rather than crashing on `git diff`;\n      verified by `pytest` (`test_first_push_zero_sha_ref_selects_nothing_without_crashing`).\n- [x] The command produces a selection with no CI environment variables set; verified by a\n      `pytest` subprocess test run with a cleared environment.\n- [x] The workflow file passes the repository's existing actionlint check; verified by\n      `pytest` over that node.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` pass; a rubric-touching range selects only the\naffected criteria; a non-rubric range selects none; `docs/exit-codes.md` documents the new\nmode.\n\n## Budget\n\n**Hard cap $25**, covering verification runs while developing this child. Steady-state cost\nafterwards is zero unless a rubric changes, at which point one criterion runs.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/changed_criteria.py","reason":"Shared engine function mapping a changed-file set to the criterion ids whose rubric files it touches."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","reason":"Expose the selection as `rebar criteria eval --changed-since <ref>`, calling the shared engine function rather than reimplementing the mapping."},{"path":".github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml","reason":"Add the change-triggered job as a thin caller, and keep the new specs out of the weekly live sweep's resolved list."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_changed_criteria.py","reason":"Subprocess tests over seeded temporary git repositories for the selection, the empty case, the unmappable rubric path and the no-CI-environment case."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm_eval.py","reason":"Make the `criteria eval` positional criterion_id OPTIONAL and mutually exclusive with the new `--changed-since <ref>` flag; neither given still yields exit 2, preserving the documented contract."},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"Update the `criteria` row to document the `--changed-since` selection mode: prints selected ids and exits 0; an unmappable rubric path is named on stderr and still exits 0; empty/missing id (neither form) still exits 2."},{"path":".github/mechanism-baseline.json","reason":"Register the new non-blocking eval-changed-rubrics ci_gate job (from prompt-eval.yml) in the mechanism baseline so the mechanism-delta ratchet passes."},{"path":"scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py","reason":"Exclude the new non-blocking (continue-on-error) eval-changed-rubrics job from the Verified-vote parity gate so it cannot redden main."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87"],["parent","65dd-e93b-666a-4caa"],["relates_to","6532-afd1-2beb-4f11"],["relates_to","be55-cb13-a241-4382"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"65dd-e93b-666a-4caa","parent_status_uuid":"f09b9b1a-75c6-44d0-883c-5fc1d37d92fe","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["plan-review","evals","ci","budget"],"ticket_id":"5169-ab69-9c23-4f8b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Run a criterion's fixtures when its rubric changes, keeping them off the weekly live sweep","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2dbce9f2-bdb5-4479-9551-42de4335b8a2","a555b0e8-08e7-4fb6-bca4-d6bb905596f0","875c5f67-5a24-4c78-84bc-956012eb3c29","5c468c0c-dda7-4687-a8f6-d24a20ec9562","dcf3db87-0b9d-4a9f-9861-e2582f4e2aee","806d2ab8-4323-430e-8138-e71dab083fe3","29f18fdb-f063-4d0e-9774-b1421a81886c","bf8a6f8b-abcb-4845-9035-d5fc8ff91e9b","6f6475f6-8334-429b-9532-8e5875d08890","c756b6fb-ddef-4208-b7c5-06b07adbf234","f03095d9-2f26-41fe-b327-a731c711bef1","0b97133c-0d68-431d-a785-2b7a347ce8ce","f09b9b1a-75c6-44d0-883c-5fc1d37d92fe","9bb57191-fb13-4f1a-b8c2-a0e84e9f03ff"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788542378900487001,"uuid":"f44790d8-41c4-4c14-a110-a8f0fa4f36bf"}